      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "About the theme macro",
          "description": "",
          "links": [],
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "transformations": [],
              "queryOptions": {}
            }
          },
          "vizConfig": {
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "group": "text",
            "version": "13.2.0-local",
            "spec": {
              "options": {
                "code": {
                  "language": "plaintext",
                  "showLineNumbers": false,
                  "showMiniMap": false
                },
                "content": "## The `__theme` macro\n\nReads any value from the current Grafana theme, so content follows light and dark themes without hardcoded colors.\n\nYou are viewing the **${__theme.name}** theme (mode: `${__theme.colors.mode}`). Press `c` then `t` to switch themes and watch every panel on this dashboard update.\n\n| Write | Gets | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| <code>$&#123;__theme.colors.primary.text&#125;</code> | a color | <span style=\"color: ${__theme.colors.primary.text}\">${__theme.colors.primary.text}</span> |\n| <code>$&#123;__theme.typography.fontFamilyMonospace&#125;</code> | a font stack | <span style=\"font-family: ${__theme.typography.fontFamilyMonospace}\">${__theme.typography.fontFamilyMonospace}</span> |\n| <code>$&#123;__theme.typography.fontSize&#125;</code>px | a number, add the unit yourself | ${__theme.typography.fontSize}px |\n| <code>$&#123;__theme.typography.size.lg&#125;</code> | a px size | <span style=\"font-size: ${__theme.typography.size.lg}\">${__theme.typography.size.lg}</span> |\n| <code>$&#123;__theme.shape.radius.default&#125;</code> | a CSS length | ${__theme.shape.radius.default} |\n\nOnly plain values resolve. Objects (<code>$&#123;__theme.colors&#125;</code>) and functions (<code>$&#123;__theme.spacing&#125;</code>) stay as literal text, so a typo is easy to spot: ${__theme.colors.nope}\n\nThe macro is global: it works in any panel, title, link or query, not only in the Text panel.\n",
                "mode": "markdown"
              },
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-2": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Semantic colors",
          "description": "colors.<color>.<shade>",
